WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.900 --> 00:00:04.571
Compound growth sounds
complicated. It isn't.

2
00:00:04.651 --> 00:00:07.950
Let's walk through it with $100 a month.

3
00:00:09.250 --> 00:00:13.215
Compound growth means your gains
can earn gains of their own.

4
00:00:13.295 --> 00:00:18.278
If an investment grows this year,
next year that growth can grow too.

5
00:00:18.358 --> 00:00:23.228
Over many years, that adds up,
which is why time matters so much.

6
00:00:24.528 --> 00:00:26.598
Here's a hypothetical.

7
00:00:26.678 --> 00:00:31.427
One person puts in $100
a month from age 25.

8
00:00:31.507 --> 00:00:33.280
Another starts at 30.

9
00:00:33.360 --> 00:00:36.249
Both assume a steady 6% a year.

10
00:00:36.329 --> 00:00:41.410
By 65, the early starter
has put in $48,000,

11
00:00:41.450 --> 00:00:47.051
and the balance could be about $191,700.

12
00:00:47.131 --> 00:00:51.804
The later starter could
have about $138,000.

13
00:00:51.884 --> 00:01:00.728
Waiting five years means $6,000 less put
in, but about $53,700 less at the end.

14
00:01:02.028 --> 00:01:03.321
Now the catch.

15
00:01:03.401 --> 00:01:07.422
Real markets don't move in a
smooth line like this chart.

16
00:01:07.502 --> 00:01:12.821
Some years they fall, sometimes a
lot, and recovering can take years.

17
00:01:12.901 --> 00:01:17.179
A steady 6% is a
simplification, not a promise.

18
00:01:18.479 --> 00:01:19.892
Quick recap.

19
00:01:19.972 --> 00:01:22.958
Growth can earn growth
of its own over time.

20
00:01:23.038 --> 00:01:26.384
Starting earlier gives
money more years to grow.

21
00:01:26.464 --> 00:01:28.575
And growth is never promised.

22
00:01:28.655 --> 00:01:31.035
Examples are hypothetical.

23
00:01:31.115 --> 00:01:36.230
Investments can fall in value,
including the money you put in.

24
00:01:37.530 --> 00:01:38.579
Quick check.

25
00:01:38.659 --> 00:01:41.053
What does compound growth mean?

26
00:01:41.133 --> 00:01:45.598
Answer three short questions below
the video to finish the lesson.

27
00:01:46.898 --> 00:01:48.897
Now try the calculator.

28
00:01:48.977 --> 00:01:53.180
Compare starting at your age
with starting five years later.
